-- title:
--   Unique centre place of a crossing-presented node
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ an element lying in $A$, and write $A_0 = A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$); assume $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian local, has algebraically closed residue field, and that every element of $A$ differs from some element of $A_0$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$. Regard the field `fieldBar q M'` (an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in the Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, for level $q^2M'$ and the level structure `levelH q M'`) as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. The assertion is then: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ such that the join of $F_0$ with the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is everything, and such that for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every family $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a$ of elements of the join of $F_0$ with $k_0(K')$ in `fieldBar q M'`, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$; for every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ which is a discrete valuation ring, agrees with $A$ on $k_0$ (an element of $k_0$ lies in $A$ iff its image lies in $W_0$) and has maximal ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$; for every noetherian local subring $O$ of $F_0$ contained in $W_0$ and agreeing with $A$ on $k_0$, such that every $f \in O$ differs from the image of some element of $A \cap k_0$ by a non-unit of $O$, and such that every $f \in F_0$ satisfies $fh = g$ for some $g, h \in O$ with $h \neq 0$; for every $E_0 \ge 1$ with the image of $\pi_0$ in $O$, every $c_x, c_y \in O$, unit $u$ of $O$, ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` of the adic completion $\widehat{A_0}$ with parameter $\widehat{\pi_0}^{\,E_0}$, i.e. $\widehat{A_0}[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi_0^{E_0})$, and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that model, subject to $c_x c_y = \pi_0^{E_0} u$, to $\iota$ sending constants from $A \cap k_0$ to the corresponding `const`, to $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U \cdot U$ and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V \cdot V$, and to $c_y$ lying in the maximal ideal of $W_0$ while $c_x$ does not; and finally for every field $FSS$ which is an algebra over the residue field of $A$ and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ to `fieldBar q M'` with values in $FSS$ (a valuation subring `R.integers` of `fieldBar q M'` meeting $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in $A$, together with a surjective homomorphism `R.residue` to $FSS$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, extending reduction on $A$, and such that every nonzero $f$ has a scalar multiple with nonzero residue) satisfying $f \in R.\mathrm{integers} \iff f \in W_0$ for $f \in F_0$ — there exists a place $nd$ of $FSS$ over the residue field of $A$, that is, a valuation subring of $FSS$ other than $FSS$ itself which contains the image of the residue field of $A$ and is a principal ideal ring, such that: $nd$ is rational, i.e. the residue field of $A$ maps onto the residue field of $nd$; the reduction `R.residue` of every element of $O$ lies in $nd$, and the reduction of every non-unit of $O$ lies in the maximal ideal of $nd$; $nd$ is the unique place of $FSS$ over the residue field of $A$ with these last two properties; the reduction of $c_y$ is $0$; and the reduction of $c_x$ has $nd$-order $1$, where the order is minus the logarithm of the associated height-one adic valuation.
--
--   This is the node-point statement for the reduction of the modular curve of full level $q^2M'$: it locates, on the reduction of a regular prolongation, the unique rational centre place of a node presented by a crossing model $\widehat{A_0}[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi_0^{E_0})$, and records that the $V$-coordinate reduces to zero while the $U$-coordinate reduces to a uniformiser at that place. It is used in the construction of the layered node rings attached to nodes of the Igusa-type reduction, in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_nodeCentre_igusaEnd_layeredNodeRings_of_mem_nodes_igusaSep_layerExponent_of_prime`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_nodeCentre_igusaEnd_layeredNodeRings_of_mem_nodes_igusaSep_layerExponent_of_prime) and its variant with prescribed width.
